.TH IFTTTNOTIFY 1 "September 2026" "iftttnotify 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iftttnotify \- send IFTTT Webhooks notifications from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iftttnotify
.RI [ options ] " value1 " [ value2 " [ value3 ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iftttnotify
sends up to three values to an IFTTT Webhooks event. It reads the Webhooks key
from
.B IFTTT_WEBHOOKS_KEY
or, in order, from
.IR ~/.ifttt-webhooks-key ,
.IR ~/.config/ifttt-webhooks-key ,
or
.IR /etc/ifttt-webhooks-key .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-e " event"
Set the IFTTT trigger event. The default is
.BR notify .
.TP
.B \-g
Print the configured Webhooks key.
.TP
.B \-h
Show help.
.TP
.B \-m
Also send a copy of the notification message to the local mail inbox.
.TP
.B \-r
Use the
.B rich_notify
event.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The IFTTT request succeeded.
.TP
.B 16
Invalid command-line option or command.
.TP
.B 17
A required executable is missing.
.TP
.B 18
No IFTTT Webhooks key was configured.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
IFTTT_WEBHOOKS_KEY=... iftttnotify "Build complete" "main" "success"
iftttnotify -e deploy "Production deploy complete"
iftttnotify -r "A richer notification"
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1)
